Retargeted from 8.2 to 6.4 and rebased there. The inconsistency reproduces identically on 6.4, so that is the oldest affected maintained branch:

```
                               ByteString     CodePointString    UnicodeString
indexOf, offset past end       ValueError     ValueError         null
indexOf, offset before start   ValueError     ValueError         null
indexOfLast, past end          ValueError     ValueError         ValueError
indexOfLast, before start      ValueError     ValueError         null
```

Treating it as a bugfix rather than a behaviour change seems right: the return type is already `?int`, only some of the implementations honour it, and the ones that throw do so because a PHP 8 migration was left half done. The change is also permissive, so code that catches the `ValueError` today keeps working.

Restoring the three sources and keeping the new provider rows fails with the underlying errors, so the added cases prove the fix:

```
ValueError: strpos(): Argument #3 ($offset) must be contained in argument #1 ($haystack)
ValueError: stripos(): Argument #3 ($offset) must be contained in argument #1 ($haystack)
```

`git merge-tree` against 7.4, 8.1 and 8.2 is conflict free, so the merge up should be uneventful.

Also dropped the four repeated `// out-of-range offsets make the underlying PHP functions throw a ValueError` comments in the providers: the expected `null` next to an offset of 10 on a three-character string says it already.

Suite: String 2380 tests, green.
